Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

EXT. INDUSTRIAL ESTATE - SUNDAY - NIGHT

On Reyes's operational phone: POSSIBLE SITE. NO APPROACH UNTIL VERIFIED. Voss replies: HOLD. TWENTY-FIVE MINUTES.

Reyes studies Elias's photograph. DRIVER. He types VISUAL ONLY.

He checks the storage row and rear fence. Warm vent. Recent mud. Light beneath the lock-up door. His phone vibrates; he silences it. He forces the lock before backup arrives.

INT. LOCK-UP - CONTINUOUS

Empty camp bed. Coat. Boots. Reyes moves away from the doorway. Elias comes through the partition.

Reyes blocks him and drives him into the wall. Dust falls. Elias's shoulder takes the impact. The fight is difficult, brief and close.

REYES
You should have kept driving.

Beside the workbench Reyes loses his footing. The struggle ends on the concrete below the old nail. His breath stops. A train rattles the roof.

Elias kneels until it passes. Standing too fast, he grips the wall. He looks from the body to the exit, then at his hands. They shake. He lets them shake.

Reyes's phone lights: VOSS CALLING. The unlocked thread names Voss and Vale; markers show them approaching. Elias writes the identifiers on a page, powers the phone down and shields it in a tool pouch. Wallet and keys remain. He leaves through the adjoining unit.

INT./EXT. FARMHOUSE/LOCK-UP - LATE NIGHT

Zoe watches reflections, distinguishes rain on the shed from an approach, checks their loose-stone signal. The timer runs.

Voss stops at the open lock-up threshold. Calls Vale.

VOSS
Reyes is down. No. Not alive. The phone's gone.

Vale arrives. They document the scene. Her eye catches the packet of mints in Reyes's coat, then the old nail and opened partition.

VALE
The room didn't attack his competence.

VOSS
We should have pulled him after the market.

VALE
Mac gave us a description.

VOSS
And we didn't examine it.

INT. FARMHOUSE - EARLY MONDAY

Elias returns before Zoe's deadline. Torn shoulder, spreading bruise. She sits with the backpack on her lap. He places the shielded phone at the far end of the table.

ZOE
Did you kill him?

ELIAS
Yes.

ZOE
Was there another way?

ELIAS
Before tonight? Probably. Inside the room, no.

ZOE
You designed the room.

ELIAS
Yes.

She moves the backpack to the floor.

ZOE
You told me he had a choice.

ELIAS
I was wrong.

ZOE
That doesn't make you less wrong.

ELIAS
No.

His hand trembles once against the table.

ZOE
Are you frightened?

ELIAS
Of how quickly it became familiar.

She opens the notebook but doesn't write.

ZOE
Who did you teach before me? What was his name?

ELIAS
Not tonight. Tomorrow.

She neither assures him of trust nor leaves. Both stay in the dark kitchen with what he has said.
